{
  "sn12.33:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.33 ",
  "sn12.33:0.2": "4. Kaḷāra the Aristocrat ",
  "sn12.33:0.3": "Grounds for Knowledge ",
  "sn12.33:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.33:1.2": "“Mendicants, I will teach forty-four grounds for knowledge. ",
  "sn12.33:1.3": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "sn12.33:1.4": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn12.33:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn12.33:2.1": "“And what are the forty-four grounds for knowledge? ",
  "sn12.33:2.2": "Knowledge of old age and death, knowledge of the origin of old age and death, knowledge of the cessation of old age and death, and knowledge of the practice that leads to the cessation of old age and death. ",
  "sn12.33:2.3": "Knowledge of rebirth … ",
  "sn12.33:2.4": "Knowledge of continued existence … ",
  "sn12.33:2.5": "Knowledge of grasping … ",
  "sn12.33:2.6": "Knowledge of craving … ",
  "sn12.33:2.7": "Knowledge of feeling … ",
  "sn12.33:2.8": "Knowledge of contact … ",
  "sn12.33:2.9": "Knowledge of the six sense fields … ",
  "sn12.33:2.10": "Knowledge of name and form … ",
  "sn12.33:2.11": "Knowledge of consciousness … ",
  "sn12.33:2.12": "Knowledge of choices, knowledge of the origin of choices, knowledge of the cessation of choices, and knowledge of the practice that leads to the cessation of choices. ",
  "sn12.33:2.13": "These are called the forty-four grounds for knowledge. ",
  "sn12.33:3.1": "And what is old age and death? ",
  "sn12.33:3.2": "The old age, decrepi